247
00:15:27,820 --> 00:15:32,320
Can I please have your attention
calling all passengers at the lagoon?

248
00:15:32,680 --> 00:15:34,980
Any lagoon passengers out there?

249
00:15:35,140 --> 00:15:37,860
We have a message from Signore Zuccaro.

250
00:15:38,540 --> 00:15:41,497
Please make your way to the
guard shack on the double.

251
00:15:41,580 --> 00:15:45,380
I repeat, calling all
passengers at the lagoon.

252
00:15:45,720 --> 00:15:50,197
We have a message from Signore Zuccaro
that requires your immediate attention.

253
00:15:50,280 --> 00:15:53,456
So he's playing it safe and
ignoring the announcement.

254
00:15:54,180 --> 00:15:56,157
Or he thinks they've found the loot,

255
00:15:56,240 --> 00:16:00,257
and he's about to jump out and
celebrate being 10 billion lira richer.

256
00:16:00,340 --> 00:16:01,399
It's all a gamble.

257
00:16:01,640 --> 00:16:04,017
Whoever hears the
announcement and heads to the

258
00:16:04,100 --> 00:16:07,240
guard shack to get their
message is our mystery man.

259
00:16:08,220 --> 00:16:09,867
I'm counting on you, Giorno.

260
00:16:10,020 --> 00:16:13,667
If anyone makes a move toward
the guard shack, give me a sign.

261
00:16:14,680 --> 00:16:18,327
Whoever answers that call is
going to get a head full of lead.

262
00:16:19,040 --> 00:16:23,540
Then again, Bucciarati wants that ass
alive, so I should avoid his vitals.

263
00:16:23,760 --> 00:16:25,172
We'll see how that goes.

264
00:16:26,940 --> 00:16:27,770
Crap.

265
00:16:27,853 --> 00:16:28,817
No one wants to make a move.

266
00:16:28,900 --> 00:16:30,194
No one's heading over.

267
00:16:31,180 --> 00:16:32,010
ATTENCIONE!

268
00:16:32,093 --> 00:16:33,240
THIS IS THE LAST CALL!

269
00:16:33,720 --> 00:16:36,097
CALLING ALL PASSENGERS OF THE Lagoon!

270
00:16:36,180 --> 00:16:40,380
WE HAVE A MESSAGE FROM SENIOR
EZUCERO THAT REQUIRES YOUR ATTENTION!

271
00:16:45,680 --> 00:16:46,677
NO ONE YET!

272
00:16:46,760 --> 00:16:47,936
NOTHING'S HAPPENING!

273
00:16:48,180 --> 00:16:50,317
HE'S GOTTA BE ON THE ISLAND SOMEWHERE!

274
00:16:50,400 --> 00:16:53,341
COULD HE REALLY BE PLAYING
IT SAFE AND HIDING OUT?

275
00:16:56,940 --> 00:17:00,497
Hey, Zookero, if something happened,
why did you request an announcement?

276
00:17:00,580 --> 00:17:01,410
Is there a problem?

277
00:17:01,493 --> 00:17:02,323
Over.

278
00:17:06,360 --> 00:17:07,740
What is going on?

279
00:17:08,160 --> 00:17:10,395
No one's showing up at the damn shack.

280
00:17:14,860 --> 00:17:15,690
What?

281
00:17:15,773 --> 00:17:16,603
He's inside.

282
00:17:16,820 --> 00:17:17,777
But when did he...

283
00:17:17,860 --> 00:17:19,997
That lookout must have another entrance.

284
00:17:20,080 --> 00:17:22,609
And that bastard knew
exactly where it was.

285
00:17:23,700 --> 00:17:27,229
It's too dark to see his face,
and Mista hasn't noticed him.

286
00:17:27,760 --> 00:17:31,525
If things don't turn around, he'll
catch on to our ruse and run.

287
00:17:32,120 --> 00:17:33,720
I have to let Mista know.

288
00:17:37,860 --> 00:17:38,690
What?

289
00:17:38,773 --> 00:17:41,112
The guy from the radio is finally coming?

290
00:17:45,600 --> 00:17:46,840
Which one is it?

291
00:17:47,520 --> 00:17:49,520
Who's coming to the lookout, Chaka?

292
00:17:51,900 --> 00:17:52,740
No, Mista!

293
00:17:53,100 --> 00:17:54,865
No one's going to the lookout!

294
00:17:55,560 --> 00:17:56,760
He's already inside!

295
00:17:57,260 --> 00:17:58,220
Just stay put!

296
00:18:00,200 --> 00:18:01,840
The enemy is by the window!

297
00:18:12,240 --> 00:18:13,157
This bastard!

298
00:18:13,240 --> 00:18:15,260
He's one of Bucciarati's goons!

299
00:18:16,120 --> 00:18:19,397
Zucchero was supposed to get rid
of him while he was on that boat!

300
00:18:19,480 --> 00:18:21,160
Mista! Behind you!

301
00:18:21,440 --> 00:18:25,940
The target is on the radio!
Mista! Damn it! He can't hear me!

302
00:18:27,040 --> 00:18:28,300
I've got no choice!

303
00:18:29,060 --> 00:18:30,880
On your left! Mista!

304
00:18:31,080 --> 00:18:32,609
He's already on the radio!

305
00:18:47,720 --> 00:18:50,440
Come on, pass, pass, pass!

306
00:18:51,680 --> 00:18:52,510
Right.

307
00:18:52,920 --> 00:18:54,200
Now go, six bullets.

308
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:57,480
Here we go!

309
00:19:05,320 --> 00:19:06,150
Yeah!

310
00:19:06,440 --> 00:19:07,270
Yeah!

311
00:19:07,353 --> 00:19:08,183
Whoo!

312
00:19:15,880 --> 00:19:16,710
Yeah!

313
00:19:19,200 --> 00:19:20,780
Yeah! Yeah! Yeah!

314
00:19:21,340 --> 00:19:22,170
Yeah!

315
00:19:22,253 --> 00:19:23,083
Yeah!

316
00:19:23,166 --> 00:19:23,996
Yeah!

317
00:19:24,079 --> 00:19:24,909
Yeah! Did he get him? Uh-huh.

318
00:19:25,660 --> 00:19:26,490
Ugh.

319
00:19:26,700 --> 00:19:27,530
Hey!

320
00:19:27,613 --> 00:19:28,595
Who the hell are you?

321
00:19:28,700 --> 00:19:31,180
Also, what was that noise? Gunshots.

322
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:33,540
Sorry, did I disturb you?

323
00:19:33,760 --> 00:19:37,819
Because I'm sure it wasn't as bad
as anything you hear in the movies.

324
00:19:37,960 --> 00:19:40,489
But if my work really
disturbed your day...

325
00:19:41,120 --> 00:19:43,257
I'm in the middle of something right now,

326
00:19:43,340 --> 00:19:46,340
and I'll address all your
complaints once I'm done.

327
00:19:48,560 --> 00:19:50,148
Giorno's always in a hurry.

328
00:19:54,560 --> 00:19:55,678
Rear entrance, huh?

329
00:19:56,440 --> 00:20:01,097
He must have made his way in through that
door in order to use the radio unnoticed.

330
00:20:01,180 --> 00:20:03,557
Either he's taking caution
to a whole new level?

331
00:20:03,640 --> 00:20:05,537
or the sneaky bastard has a weird habit.

332
00:20:05,620 --> 00:20:08,679
of always trying to enter
buildings on the down low.

333
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:13,240
Regardless, that was some
killer work, Buds! Yay! Come on!

334
00:20:13,580 --> 00:20:15,140
We got his leg!

335
00:20:15,400 --> 00:20:17,980
We got that right leg good, didn't we?

336
00:20:18,140 --> 00:20:20,320
Yeah, I'd say you nailed the sucker.

337
00:20:20,600 --> 00:20:22,012
He's not going anywhere.

338
00:20:28,220 --> 00:20:30,457
The usual tourists out front.

339
00:20:30,540 --> 00:20:33,017
Back here is a friggin' cliff.

340
00:20:33,100 --> 00:20:34,737
No way he climbed that thing!

341
00:20:34,820 --> 00:20:37,337
Must be stumbling around here somewhere.

342
00:20:37,420 --> 00:20:39,240
Show yourself, coward!

343
00:20:48,160 --> 00:20:50,120
He must be hiding in that truck.

344
00:20:50,540 --> 00:20:52,200
If he's a stand user,

345
00:20:52,560 --> 00:20:56,384
then he's more than likely a
close-range one with striking power.

346
00:20:57,220 --> 00:20:59,120
If he were the long-range type,

347
00:20:59,260 --> 00:21:02,731
it's safe to say he would have
attacked me a long time ago.

348
00:21:03,100 --> 00:21:06,617
Now that he's got a bum leg, he's not
going to be traveling any kind of distance,

349
00:21:06,700 --> 00:21:09,000
so he's probably laying a trap for me.

350
00:21:09,240 --> 00:21:13,005
I bet he's behind this truck
waiting to lure me in for the kill.

351
00:21:13,540 --> 00:21:17,128
Well, it's not like he could
hurt me even if I did get close.

352
00:21:19,340 --> 00:21:21,300
He's probably just beyond there.

353
00:21:21,660 --> 00:21:25,072
But I'm still in the dark as
far as what his stand can do.

354
00:21:25,520 --> 00:21:28,617
Going in without backup would
be risky, to say the least.

355
00:21:28,700 --> 00:21:31,040
I should wait for Giorno and...

356
00:21:32,160 --> 00:21:32,990
Shit.

357
00:21:33,073 --> 00:21:34,352
Guess that option's out.

358
00:21:34,660 --> 00:21:36,836
So the Strontos in the driver's seat.

359
00:21:36,980 --> 00:21:38,417
He must have jump-started the engine.

360
00:21:38,500 --> 00:21:41,460
I can't let him escape
now, especially here.

361
00:21:42,560 --> 00:21:43,780
Damn this prick!

362
00:21:44,080 --> 00:21:47,997
I still don't know what the guy
looks like, and neither does Giorno!

363
00:21:48,080 --> 00:21:50,557
His stand will have to
stay a mystery for now.

364
00:21:50,640 --> 00:21:53,111
This is for the 10 billion and Bucciarati!

365
00:21:59,160 --> 00:21:59,990
Die!

366
00:22:03,940 --> 00:22:04,770
Mista.

367
00:22:09,820 --> 00:22:12,757
Every time I close my eyes.

368
00:22:12,840 --> 00:22:16,040
I wake up feeling so horny.

369
00:22:16,860 --> 00:22:19,877
I can't get you out of my mind.

370
00:22:19,960 --> 00:22:23,357
Since you'll be all I see.

371
00:22:23,440 --> 00:22:26,437
I would give anything.

372
00:22:26,520 --> 00:22:30,497
Just to make you understand me.

373
00:22:30,580 --> 00:22:34,817
I don't give a damn about nothing else.

374
00:22:34,900 --> 00:22:38,397
Freaking you is all I need.

375
00:22:38,480 --> 00:22:41,337
I need your mind.

376
00:22:41,420 --> 00:22:43,200
I need your mind.

377
00:22:45,420 --> 00:22:48,040
Tonight you got my time.

378
00:22:50,460 --> 00:22:52,600
I'll give it to you.

379
00:22:53,280 --> 00:22:56,020
Tonight you won't be sorry.

380
00:22:57,900 --> 00:22:59,877
I'll give it to you.

381
00:22:59,960 --> 00:23:02,777
Tonight you got my mind.

382
00:23:02,860 --> 00:23:07,460
I've got my mind, all I
want to do is free to you.

383
00:23:07,680 --> 00:23:09,400
What must I say?

384
00:23:09,840 --> 00:23:10,860
Tell me.

385
00:23:11,240 --> 00:23:12,837
What must I do?

386
00:23:12,920 --> 00:23:14,680
What must I do?

387
00:23:14,840 --> 00:23:20,720
To show how much I'm going to free to you.

388
00:23:20,920 --> 00:23:23,760
What must I say?

389
00:23:25,040 --> 00:23:27,240
What must I do?

390
00:23:28,860 --> 00:23:29,860
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

391
00:23:30,060 --> 00:23:32,760
To show how much I'm going to free to you.

392
00:23:32,860 --> 00:23:34,360
I'm gonna break it.

393
00:24:10,700 --> 00:24:11,900
Thank you.
